      "semantics": "There is no STRING type, quoted-string syntax, free identifier, free text, or comment syntax. DATE_LITERAL is valid only when its day exists in its stated proleptic-Gregorian month and year. URL_LITERAL is an absolute HTTPS URL under the complete grammar above; no external URL standard is invoked. PATH_LITERAL is a nonempty normalized relative path with no empty, dot, or dot-dot segment. NAME_LITERAL is one atomic proper-name token and cannot contain spaces or prose syntax. Every ontology symbol is legal only if an exact corresponding entry exists in the complete glossary; matching a namespace shape alone is insufficient. Handles are canonical: assign $v1 to the ENTRYPOINT target, then assign increasing handles at each declaration, parameter, result, LET, loop, or turn introduction in preorder source order. A later reference must use that allocated handle.",
