 "summary": "This revision replaces free identifiers, strings, comments, and open prefix acceptance with glossary-governed handles, atomic literals, ontology entries, and typed symbolic code trees. It also gives Actions, Utterances, Generation, Tasks, and Conversations one canonical symbolic representation for executable work, generated artifacts, revisions, and follow-up questions.",
 "note_position": "comply",
 "note_argument": "All expression tokens are either structural symbols defined by Types & Lexicon, canonical handles, exact atomic literals, or symbols whose corresponding complete glossary entry defines their category, schema, type, and canonical attribute order. No quoted prose, unrestricted identifier, comment channel, or prefix-only namespace rule remains.",
 "foundations_overview": "BrainCode is a closed, typed symbolic language. Source consists only of finite structural symbols, canonical local handles, exact atomic literals, and glossary-defined ontology symbols. Descriptive meaning is carried by typed propositions and code trees whose constructors, fields, values, and ordering are defined in the glossary; natural-language text is never a source payload. A complete glossary is normative: an ontology-shaped spelling is legal only when its exact entry exists there, and every operation, intent, attribute, relation, value, entity, role, and code atom is resolved through that entry.",
