   "model (OpenAssistant/oasst-sft-4-pythia-12b-epoch-3.5, score=82): Here's a recipe for high protein flatbread that has received high reviews:\n\nIngredients:\n\n1 cup whole wheat flour\n1 teaspoon baking powder\n1/2 teaspoon salt\n1 cup Greek yogurt\n2/3 cup plain yogurt\n1 egg\n2 tablespoons olive oil\n1/2 cup almond flour\n1/2 teaspoon garlic powder\n1/2 teaspoon onion powder\n1/2 teaspoon paprika\n\nInstructions:\n\n1. In a large bowl, combine the flour, baking powder, and salt.\n2. In a separate bowl, combine the Greek yogurt and plain yogurt.\n3. In a third bowl, whisk together the egg and olive oil.\n4. Gradually pour the wet ingredients into the dry ingredients and mix until a smooth dough forms.\n5. Spread the dough onto a lightly floured surface and roll out to about 1/4 inch thick.\n6. Cut the dough into desired shapes, such as rect",
   "model (OpenAssistant/oasst-sft-4-pythia-12b-epoch-3.5, score=20): You can use a pizza crust recipe to make a pizza with high protein content. Here's an example recipe:\n\nIngredients:\n\n• 1 cup all-purpose flour\n• 1 teaspoon active dry yeast\n• 1 teaspoon baking powder\n• 1 teaspoon salt\n• 1/2 cup warm water\n\nInstructions:\n\n1. In a large bowl, combine the flour, yeast, baking powder, and salt.\n2. Gradually add the warm water and mix until a smooth dough forms.\n3. Knead the dough for 5-10 minutes until it becomes smooth and elastic.\n4. Place the dough in a greased bowl, cover with plastic wrap, and let it rise in a warm place for 1 hour or until doubled in size.\n5. Punch down the dough and shape it into a circle.\n6. Preheat the oven to 425°F and grease a 9x13 inch baking dish.\n7. Transfer",
   "user (None, score=None): how much protein is in these recipes",
   "model (OpenAssistant/oasst-sft-4-pythia-12b-epoch-3.5, score=25): I'm sorry, I don't know the exact amount of protein in these recipes, as it's not included in the ingredients. You'll need to check the nutrition information on the manufacturer's website or nutrition information provided by the restaurant to determine the protein content.",
   "model (OpenAssistant/oasst-sft-4-pythia-12b-epoch-3.5, score=72): The amount of protein in each recipe varies, depending on the ingredients used and the cooking method. However, as a general rule, Greek yogurt contains about 12-16 grams of protein per cup, while almond flour contains 8-12 grams of protein per cup. Additionally, some protein sources, such as chicken and eggs, can provide significant protein boosts. Ultimately, the key to getting the most protein from your flatbread is to balance out the amount of protein from all sources, so that your overall diet contains enough protein to meet your needs.",
