- [revise] Action: grammar `action ::= ACTION operation_symbol "(" field_list? ")" ("->" HANDLE ":" type)?` — ACTION is the only external-state construct. Its exact operation entry supplies ordered fields, field types, result type, and canonical selection rule; unknown, duplicate, missing, out-of-order, or type-incompatible fields are static errors. Source-location retrieval is op_find followed by op_pick_up before any possession-sensitive action. A goal phrase such as ready-for-coffee canonically decomposes, when the demonstrated trajectory supplies it, as find, pick_up, heat in microwave, remove, then place at coffee-maker spout; no invented preparation operation is permitted.
