 "foundations_overview": "BrainCode is a closed-vocabulary, typed context-free notation. Source tokens are either fixed structural symbols, exact glossary ontology members, atomic literals with fully defined forms, or canonical opaque handles. Descriptive meaning is represented by typed, ordered proposition trees rather than English text; operation, intent, attribute, value, and code-form schemas are glossary entries. TASK performs effects, CONVO records symbolic dialogue and may derive requested symbolic artifacts through GENERATE, and all references use typed handles.",
